{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_b73wxdbqg3qua4lxblt46abexw256zhdyitlck77gvufwy35zv5a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — the Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte on every path tested. **No bugs found; no changes to `translation/src/lib.rs` were needed.**\n\n## Artifacts\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `translation/SYMBOLS.md` | 10 exported symbols; C↔Rust diff **empty** |\n| `translation/ERRORS.md` | 16 rejection rows + 7 generic FFI-boundary rows, all checked |\n| `translation/CONFIGS.md` | 45 valid-config rows, all checked |\n| `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` | harness: dual `libloading` load, fd-1 stdout capture, seeded xorshift PRNG, process-wide lock (both `.so`s carry a global `static counter`) |\n| `translation/tests/phase_b_valid.rs` | 44 tests |\n| `translation/tests/phase_c_errors.rs` | 18 tests |\n| `translation/tests/phase_d_symbols.rs` | 3 tests (`nm -D` parity, `ldd -r` resolution, libc-primitive reuse) |\n| `scripts/verify.sh` | builds both libs, enumerates feature combos, runs all phases vs debug **and** release cdylib, diffs symbols |\n\n## Results — 65 tests, all passing\n\n- **Phase A**: symbol sets identical. `lib.h` declares only `charinbuf`, but `lib.c` gives external linkage to 9 helpers too — all 10 are verified, none stubbed.\n- **Phase B**: all 45 config rows pass, with ~15k randomized inputs (seed `0x2024C0FFEE000001`). Both return value *and* captured stdout compared byte-for-byte. Covers `memchr` sign-extension for high-bit `char`, first-vs-last-vs-truncated matches, embedded-NUL targets, signed-overflow wraparound in mode 3, and the `counter = 0` reset at `charinbuf` entry.\n- **Phase C**: all 16 error rows pass, asserting the *same* sentinel (`-1` / `NULL` / `0`), not just \"both failed\". Includes out-of-range enum-like `mode` values (`INT_MIN`, `-1`, `5`, `INT_MAX`) and the `validate_uint16_range` inclusive boundaries.\n- **Phase D**: `nm -D` diff empty; `ldd -r` clean on both; Rust imports libc's own `printf`/`malloc`/`free`/`memchr`/`strlen`/`strcpy`, so formatting and heap ownership are identical.\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Feature combos**: `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` table, so the only combinations are default and `--no-default-features`; both run in `verify.sh`.\n- **No binary target** (`add_library(SHARED)` / `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`), so stdout is diffed at the FFI level instead of via a driver.\n- **Also passes against the C rebuilt at `-O3`**, so the mode-3 signed-overflow agreement isn't an artifact of the default unoptimized build.\n- Three `ERRORS.md` rows (malloc failure in `create_buffer` / mode 2, and mode 4's not-found arm) are **unreachable by construction** in the C — I marked them as contract tests that assert the sibling reachable path plus the NULL-producing sibling, rather than claiming a real trigger.\n- Tests require `-- --test-threads=1` (baked into `verify.sh`): fd 1 and the `static counter` are process-global. `--offline` is used since crates.io is unreachable from the sandbox; `libloading 0.8.9` was already in the local cargo cache."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1044,"cache_read_input_tokens":88506,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1044,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c20e836f-61f0-4665-827a-67b0c0710ad1","uuid":"16769e53-a165-43f0-8612-785fa21bccf7","timestamp":"2026-09-05T13:36:00.257Z"}
